1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,710
When a Set turns Yes, does anything different tend to happen next,

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:05,612
compared with ordinary days?

3
00:00:06,072 --> 00:00:10,468
Each time a Set first turns Yes, we look at the next ten daily candles.

4
00:00:10,518 --> 00:00:12,450
We compare them with ordinary days:

5
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:16,898
the same asset, the same year, and the same side of its long-term average.

6
00:00:16,948 --> 00:00:24,459
Twenty-five coins and sixty-one large US equities, from 2014 to October 2024.

7
00:00:24,925 --> 00:00:27,508
Every provided Set carries the result.

8
00:00:27,558 --> 00:00:30,332
Open more, and the last line is What followed.

9
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:32,489
Tap it for the numbers.

10
00:00:32,539 --> 00:00:36,210
Breakout with volume turned Yes almost nineteen hundred times.

11
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:40,405
Price rose a typical move before falling one fifty-one percent of the time,

12
00:00:40,425 --> 00:00:43,002
against fifty percent on comparable days.

13
00:00:43,449 --> 00:00:46,096
Every study ends in one of four verdicts:

14
00:00:46,146 --> 00:00:47,747
too few to judge,

15
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,441
no clear difference,

16
00:00:49,491 --> 00:00:51,626
some difference, not established,

17
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:53,661
or a consistent difference.

18
00:00:54,116 --> 00:00:56,827
Most simple setups show no clear difference.

19
00:00:56,877 --> 00:01:01,678
That's an honest, useful answer: they describe a situation; they don't predict one.

20
00:01:02,131 --> 00:01:04,628
Trend alignment is the interesting one.

21
00:01:04,678 --> 00:01:07,127
After the daily and weekly trends first agree,

22
00:01:07,147 --> 00:01:10,077
price did a little worse than on comparable days.

23
00:01:10,127 --> 00:01:13,926
Often the weekly trend confirms a move after much of it has happened.

24
00:01:14,383 --> 00:01:16,603
Your own Sets can be studied too.

25
00:01:16,653 --> 00:01:19,982
Open one in Signal Sets, and tap Study this Set.

26
00:01:20,032 --> 00:01:23,106
It runs in the background, usually within the hour.
